1.FULL BACKUP: 
   ## It will take the backup of whole db including all datafiles and logfiles nd also committed , uncommitted data.
   ## after every successful full backup, The DCM pages will be reset automatically.  ( DCM=Differential changed map )

How to take full backup:
            Right click on DB----> Tasks ---> backup
            default loc: C:/program files/microsoft sql server/MSSQL 15.MSSQLSERVER/MSSQL/Backup
Media Options:
Backup set will expire: after=0 days
compression: 
#### ( to enable compression settings ) ####
     serving settings
     go to sql server--->properties---->DB settings
                                     (  check box)--compression bkp at serevr level.

----------------------------------------------------------
script: Backup database <db name> to disk= <'file name.bak'>
---------------------------------------------------------


2. Differential backup:
   ### These backups are Cumulative backups, It will take all changes since last full bkp.
  ---script: Backup database <db name> to disk= <'file name.bak'> with differential

3. T-log/Transaction log Backup:
  ### These are Incremental bkps, It will take only logfiles.

4.Tail log bkp:
  ## It will take the backup from last Transaction log Backup
  ## If db is in (Recovery= simple) simple mode, we can't take tail log bkps.
  ## We can take these bkps,if it is in only full recovery model. ( recovery=full) 
  ------ script: Backup database <db name> to disk= <'file name.bak'> with no_truncate-----

5. Copy only full bkp:
   ### It will also take whole db including all datafiles and logfiles,but it won't touch/reset the DCM pages.
                  ( These bkps we will take only in middle of backup startegy )
------ script: Backup database <db name> to disk= <'file name.bak'> with copy_only-----

